-First, login to a free ASW account. 
-Search for EC2, select a specific region, and then click “Launch instance.”  
-Now, we are creating a Linux instance, click “Launch without a walkthrough.”  


-Name and tags: Enter any server name of your choice.Under Application and OS Images (Amazon Machine Image), select the operating system you want to use, for example, Ubuntu OS.
 
-Key Pair (Login): Click “Create a new key pair” and enter any name, for example, My-fast-key. Then click “Create key pair.” The key file will be automatically downloaded your Downloads folder. 
-Finally, click “Launch instance.” The virtual server will then be created. 
-Then, we need to connect to the server. Select the server and click “Connect.” 
-Now, connect to the server using the SSH client and click “Connect.” 


-Then, copy the 4th number is under “Connect to your instance using its Public DNS.” Open Command Prompt (CMD) on your system and type:
